    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Interest on Other Obligations Central/State Governments’. Interest on loans notified for discharge and subsequently paid (except payments which are barred by limitation) should be debited to a separate sub head ‘interest on loans in course of discharge’ under the minor head ‘Payment of interest’, if time barred as well as on loans if paid after the expiry of 20 years, when the loans themselves do not form part of Public debt, will be debited to the head ‘2075-Miscellaneous General Services 800- Other expenditure’. autonomous or statutory organisation. securities held in cash balance investment account. major head for each denomination of loans from each country and also for the loans from the International Banks or Institutions for each project. Additional sub-heads viz ‘Commitment Charges’ and ‘Incidental expenses’ may also be opened. The sub- head 'Incidental Expenses' would accommodate all incidental expenses including brokerages, commission etc, which do not fall under the Category of ‘Interest’ or ‘Commitment charges’. head ‘Management of small savings scheme’ below this sub major head corresponding to minor heads in the sector ‘I - Small Savings, Provident Funds etc’ in the Public Account. to States advanced up to 31-03-84 and outstanding as on 31-03-85. acquisition of special Drawing rights etc. Government'' and Note Reserve Bank of India booked under Major Head ‘6001/6003’. Treasury Bills. Other Savings Certificates’ are meant for transactions relating to State Governments. for Government employees of Civil Ministries, Department of Posts, Railways and Telecommunication. Advances from Central Government’ will continue to operate till earlier loans are fully repaid."
      }
    ]
  },
