        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Coinage Accounts have to be excluded from the general available cash balance) by credit for the opening and debit for the closing balance of each account. Principal Accounts Officer, Department of Economic Affairs, Ministry of Finance. Remittances'. Ministry of Finance Deptt. of Economic Affairs on receiving the requisite information from the Mint Master through the latter's monthly account, debiting Coinage Accounts (Part I Bronze and Copper Coinage Account) with the nominal value of coins manufactured by per contra credit to (i) the Capital head ‘4046- Capital Outlay on Currency, Coinage and Mint’ to the extent of the value of the material utilised and (ii) Coinage Accounts (Part II-Mint Profit Account) for the difference representing gross profit on manufacture. The amount of gross profit adjusted is intimated to the Principal Accounts Officer, Department of Economic Affairs, Ministry of Finance to enable them to complete part II. portion which belongs to the amount of coins issued for circulation that is passed out of Mint and Depots combined. The sum of the gross profits brought forward from follows: -"
